WEBVTT

NOTE
Descriptive captions for "Apollo 11 Activities" (NASA Kennedy Space Center, 16 July 1969).
The footage has launch-site sound and no narration, so the captions describe what is on screen.

00:00.300 --> 00:07.800
Morning, July 16, 1969.
The crew eats breakfast before launch.

00:08.100 --> 00:15.800
Neil Armstrong, Michael Collins
and Buzz Aldrin walk out in their spacesuits.

00:16.000 --> 00:23.800
They wave, then climb into the van
that takes them to the launch pad.

00:24.100 --> 00:30.800
Their Saturn V rocket waits
at Launch Pad 39A.

00:31.100 --> 00:40.800
High up the tower, the crew climbs
into the spacecraft, Columbia.

00:41.100 --> 00:46.800
In the firing room,
the launch team watches every system.

00:47.100 --> 00:54.800
The rocket stands ready
on the pad.

00:55.100 --> 01:02.800
The countdown clock:
ten minutes to go.

01:03.100 --> 01:16.300
Almost time.
Now it's your turn.
